  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n\nThe Erds minimum overlap problem seeks a step function h: [0,2] -> [0,1] with \u222bh(x)dx=1 that minimizes C5 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx. The current best bound is 0.3808, and our approach is the Harmonic Transform Optimization with Adaptive Frequency Selection. We represent solutions as periodic functions on [0,2] using a Fourier series with adaptive amplitude-frequency profiles. The key innovation is dual-frequency basis functions (f and N-f) that capture both primary structural frequency and its complementary counterpart, leveraging the beats phenomenon in signal processing to create structured patterns. This differs fundamentally from standard single-frequency representations and the parent's piecewise optimization.\n\nThe approach addresses four problem bottlenecks:\n1. **Local Convergence**: Standard methods easily get trapped\n2. **Overlap Calculation**: Reliable evaluation requires ad hoc handling\n3. **Box Constraints**: Traditional methods insufficiently stabilize function values\n4. **Resolution Dependency**: Largely disconnected representations across different n\n\nThe solution combines periodic structure exploitation with metric-induced smoothness to navigate the Poisson's problem of dimensional growth.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n\nGiven period T=2 (the domain length), express h(x) as truncated Fourier series:\n\nh(x) = a\u2080/2 + \u2211\u209a\u208c\u2081\u1d39 [a\u209a cos(2\u03c0f\u209ax) + b\u209a sin(2\u03c0f\u209ax)]\n\nWhere:\n- f bases are family duplicates chosen from two sets\n- Discrete samples at resolution n: x\u1d62 = i/n, i=0 to n-1\n- Integral constraint: \u222b\u2080\u00b2h(x)dx=1 (projects to \u2211h\u1d62/n/2)\n- Periodic extension for shifts: h(x+2)=h(x)\n- Constrained to 0\u2264h\u22641\n\nThe objective is: C5 = (2/n) \u00d7 max\u2096 |sum\u2c7c h\u2c7c(1-h\u2c7c\u208a\u2096)|\n\nWe minimize C5 using a constrained optimization in Fourier coefficients, with:\n1. Dynamic frequency selection: Basis frequencies f\u209a chosen adaptively from [0.3,0.7]\n2. Beat complementarity: Harmonies f\u209a and N-f\u209a added simultaneously\n3. Stabilizing manifold: Contribution weighting by harmonic inertia\n\nObjectives are evaluated via spectral covariance operators, with gradient projections enforced as positive definite transformations.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n\nPhase initialization:\n- Validate parent's f/n ratio (if present)\n- Set n_initial = len(initial_h_values) if available\n\nParameter setup:\n- M_max = min(n/10, 50)   - Max frequency terms\n- \u03b1_diversity = 0.8 - Diversity maintenance parameter\n\nCore optimization loop:\n\nfunction harmony_evolution(n):\n  if parent available:\n    h0 = initial_h_values\n    log(\"Using existing 700-point solution as initial guess\")\n  else:\n    h0 = np.clip(rng.normal(0.5,0.2,n),0,1)\n    sum_project(h0,n)   # Normalize integral\n\n  if integrate check: localize scientific structure\n\n  freq_bases = harmonify_spectrum(n, parent_spectrum if exists)\n  coeffs = 2*exp(-freq_bases^2/(10))  # Initial coefficient envelope\n\n  best_state = {h: h0, score: compute_c5(h0,n)}\n\n  // Phase 1: Metric-aware coordinate descent\n  for iter=1 to 150:\n      C5_val = compute_c5_with_fallback(n)   // Monitoring safety\n      if time_overhead > budget/3: exit_failure()\n\n      update_structure(freq_bases, n)   // Periodicity adaptation\n      grad_coeffs = spectral_gradient(coeffs, freq_bases)\n      \n      coeffs = clac_proximal_step(grad_coeffs, n) \n      coeffs = projection(proj_box(coeffs)[:, proj_spectral(coeffs, n)])\n\n      // With 20% probability:\n      if experimental():\n          coeffs = subspace_transfer(n)   // Fourier basis morphing\n\n      new_h = reconstruct_solution(coeffs, freq_bases, n)\n      if validate_overlap(new_h, n) improving(best_state.):\n          best_state = new_h, score\n\n      // Educed adaptation\n      if stagnation(iter): \n          coeffs = perturb_envelope(freq_bases, rand_draw_diversity())\n          freq_bases = harmonize_envelope(n)\n\n  return best_state.h, best_state.score\n\nHelper Functions:\n\nfunction harmonize_spectrum(n, base=None):\n    if base is None:\n        f_range = [0.3,0.7] with both f and N-f\n    else:\n        f_range = refine_range(base)\n    return uniform_freq_draw(n, f_range)\n\nfunction validate_overlap(h, n):\n    try:\n        corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n        c5 = (2/n)*np.max(corr)\n        return (not np.isnan(c5)) and (c5 < infinity_threshold)\n    except:\n        return False  # Fallback validation\n\nfunction project_feasible(h, n):\n    norm_1d = np.clip(h,0,1)\n    integral0 = sum(h)/n*2\n    delta = 1-integral0 last_necessary adjustment\n    return norm_1d + (1/sumexp) * where_fair_difference[n/2], n)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n\nCore search algorithm:\n\nseed_dual_arithmetic(rng) = omega + c where omega is dual-complementary base\ncosine_envelope   # Systematic falloff of harmonics \n\nFive Divine Variations to improve signal-to-overlap ratio:\n\n1. Independent Advection (stdev increased): \n   if signal_noise_ratio high, apply amplitude_jitter_armotizations)\n\n2. Timewave Quadratic (for breakthrough results):\n   transform_coeffs(coeffs, new_base = minimize_noise_table)\n\n3. Logarithmic Modulation:\n   log_coeffs = np.log(np.abs(coeffs)+1e-5)\n   resample from log space\n\n4. Harmonic Resonance Cycling:\n   enable every 5 supplements: [f=f*1.1, f=f*0.9, keep midpoints]\n\n5. Poisson Sexagesimal Adjustment:\n   use low-discrepancy sampling to explore {coeffs} simplex\n\nEach variation has its own implementation in the code. We use them in a fixed schedule:\nVariation * 0 + 1 (only once in the loop)\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n\nTime Allotment:\n5% for parameter recognition\n65% Metric Harmonization (core algorithm)\n25% Capt'n Crunch (fallbacks)\n5% Valuation Boundary enforcement\n\nDeadline monitoring:\n  Time penalties applied if:statusCodeMatches('FAILED'), i.e.\n      time estimate > earlier execution OR\n      validate_overlap times out\n\nIn each core iteration (60 seconds):\n  - Coordination must completewithin 0.8s\n  - Bio-inspired stochastic components allowed up to 5s\n  - Multiple timeout checks.Messages must be prefixed\n\n  Fallback procedure if timeline exceeded:\n      - Save best_valid seen\n      - Intercept divergOMETRY if makes progress\n      - Use edificated parents as fallback\n\n  Integral normalization failure: Automatically recovered via incremental recomposition\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n\nAt exit, validate:\n  h inside [0,1] to 1e-6 tolerance\n  integral to 1e-4 tolerance\n  C5 finite and computed by multiple metrics\n\n  Final evaluation:\n      use_discrete_dominance: fallback entire array evaluation\n\n  Return format:\n      h_array, C5, n_points (number used)\n\n  This will be formatted automatically.\n\n  All operations must be:vectorized, with minimal explicit correlation\n\n  Additional invariants:\n    - The transform procedure must preserve domain periodicity\n    - Invalid states are bounded by clipping to feasible manifold\n    - Monte-Carlo integration is used if resolution changes",
